Subject: [PATCH] pipewire: fix use-after-free between request_buffer and remove_buffer

request_buffer() runs on the steamcompmgr thread: it dequeues a pw_buffer
and only afterwards marks the matching pipewire_buffer as copying. If the
PipeWire thread handles stream_handle_remove_buffer() for that pw_buffer in
between (a consumer connecting or renegotiating, usually right after
"warning: out of buffers"), it sees copying == false and frees the
pipewire_buffer. steamcompmgr then keeps the dangling pointer, pushes it back
and dispatch_nudge() -> copy_buffer() dereferences freed memory:

  Thread "gamescope-pw" received signal SIGSEGV
  #0 copy_buffer (buffer=...) at src/pipewire.cpp:196   (pw_buffer = 0x1f0000000a)
  #1 dispatch_nudge () at src/pipewire.cpp:308
  #2 run_pipewire () at src/pipewire.cpp:660

Seen on gamescope 3.16.30 (Void Linux) when Vesktop starts or changes a
screen share through xdg-desktop-portal-gamescope. Serialize "dequeue + mark
copying" against "remove" with a mutex; pw_stream_dequeue_buffer() takes no
lock, so this cannot deadlock with the PipeWire loop.
---
--- a/src/pipewire.cpp
+++ b/src/pipewire.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 
 #include <atomic>
+#include <mutex>
 #include <thread>
 #include <vector>
 
@@ -26,6 +27,14 @@
 // Pending buffer for steamcompmgr → PipeWire
 static std::atomic<struct pipewire_buffer *> in_buffer;
 
+// request_buffer() runs on the steamcompmgr thread: it dequeues a pw_buffer and only then marks
+// its pipewire_buffer as copying. If the PipeWire thread runs stream_handle_remove_buffer() for
+// that same pw_buffer in between (e.g. while a consumer connects or renegotiates the format),
+// it sees copying == false and frees the pipewire_buffer, and steamcompmgr keeps using the freed
+// pointer until dispatch_nudge() -> copy_buffer() crashes on it. Make "dequeue + mark copying"
+// and "remove" mutually exclusive. pw_stream_dequeue_buffer() itself takes no lock.
+static std::mutex buffer_handoff_mutex;
+
 // Requested capture size
 static uint32_t s_nRequestedWidth;
 static uint32_t s_nRequestedHeight;
@@ -172,6 +181,8 @@
 
 static void request_buffer(struct pipewire_state *state)
 {
+	std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(buffer_handoff_mutex);
+
 	struct pw_buffer *pw_buffer = pw_stream_dequeue_buffer(state->stream);
 	if (!pw_buffer) {
 		pwr_log.errorf("warning: out of buffers");
@@ -595,6 +606,8 @@
 {
 	struct pipewire_buffer *buffer = (struct pipewire_buffer *) pw_buffer->user_data;
 
+	std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(buffer_handoff_mutex);
+
 	buffer->buffer = nullptr;
 
 	if (!buffer->copying) {
